ow 11).\n- `init_array`/`expand_array` size multiplications wrap `size_t` rather than trapping; the Rust `wrapping_mul` matches, verified against `SIZE_MAX/4±1`, `SIZE_MAX/2+1`, `SIZE_MAX`.\n\nOne test-harness bug I fixed (not a translation bug): tests initially failed on `matrixsum` because `matrix` is a shared process-wide global and parallel test threads were mutating it under each other; a `matrix_lock()` mutex now serializes those tests.\n\nTo prove the suite isn't vacuous, I injected 4 mutations into the Rust source (mask `0xFFF`→`0xFFFF`, `capacity*2`→`*2+1`, dropped `FLAG_DELETE`, `wrapping_mul`→`saturating_mul`) — all 4 were caught, and all were reverted (`src/lib.rs` is back to its original 291 lines)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1021,"cache_read_input_tokens":109818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1021,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309dcb71-39c7-4dff-aa9b-4efd018b7d5c","uuid":"94c6242c-854c-4770-82a7-ae397f440147","timestamp":"2026-09-05T15:13:53.513Z"}
